🔥 TOP DSA QUESTION #1 (Not in Your List)
IMPLEMENT TRIE (PREFIX TREE)

👉 Very important for FAANG, string problems, autocomplete, search engines

1️⃣ Problem Statement

Design a Trie (Prefix Tree) data structure that supports the following operations:

insert(String word) → Insert a word into the trie

search(String word) → Return true if the word exists

startsWith(String prefix) → Return true if any word starts with this prefix

Example
Trie trie = new Trie();
trie.insert("apple");
trie.search("apple");   // true
trie.search("app");     // false
trie.startsWith("app"); // true
trie.insert("app");
trie.search("app");     // true

2️⃣ Key Idea (Very Important 💡)

A Trie:

Stores words character by character

Each node represents one character

Paths from root → leaf represent a word

3️⃣ Trie Node Structure

Each Trie node contains:

children[26] → for characters a to z

isEnd → marks end of a word

4️⃣ Algorithm
➤ Insert Word

Start from root

For each character:

If child does not exist → create it

Move to next node

Mark isEnd = true

➤ Search Word

Traverse character by character

If any character missing → return false

After traversal, check isEnd

➤ Starts With

Traverse prefix

If traversal succeeds → return true

5️⃣ Java Code (Clean + Interview Ready)
class Trie {

    // Step 1: Trie Node definition
    private class TrieNode {
        TrieNode[] children;
        boolean isEnd;

        public TrieNode() {
            children = new TrieNode[26]; // a-z
            isEnd = false;
        }
    }

    private TrieNode root;

    // Step 2: Constructor
    public Trie() {
        root = new TrieNode(); // empty root
    }

    // Step 3: Insert word
    public void insert(String word) {
        TrieNode current = root;

        for (char ch : word.toCharArray()) {
            int index = ch - 'a';

            if (current.children[index] == null) {
                current.children[index] = new TrieNode();
            }

            current = current.children[index];
        }

        current.isEnd = true;
    }

    // Step 4: Search word
    public boolean search(String word) {
        TrieNode current = root;

        for (char ch : word.toCharArray()) {
            int index = ch - 'a';

            if (current.children[index] == null) {
                return false;
            }

            current = current.children[index];
        }

        return current.isEnd;
    }

    // Step 5: StartsWith prefix
    public boolean startsWith(String prefix) {
        TrieNode current = root;

        for (char ch : prefix.toCharArray()) {
            int index = ch - 'a';

            if (current.children[index] == null) {
                return false;
            }

            current = current.children[index];
        }

        return true;
    }
}

6️⃣ Line-by-Line Explanation (Very Detailed 🔍)
🔹 TrieNode Class
TrieNode[] children;
boolean isEnd;


children[26] → links to next characters

isEnd → marks end of complete word

🔹 Insert Function
TrieNode current = root;


👉 Start from root

int index = ch - 'a';


👉 Converts character to index (e.g., 'c' - 'a' = 2)

if (current.children[index] == null)
    current.children[index] = new TrieNode();


👉 Create node if character path doesn’t exist

current = current.children[index];


👉 Move to next node

current.isEnd = true;


👉 Mark end of word

🔹 Search Function
if (current.children[index] == null)
    return false;


👉 If character path missing → word not present

return current.isEnd;


👉 Ensures entire word exists (not just prefix)

🔹 StartsWith Function

Same traversal as search, but:

return true;


👉 No need to check isEnd

